<!--
    తెలుగు (Telugu) — the alarm, its notifications, and the water nudge.

    THESE ARE NOT SELECTED BY THE DEVICE LOCALE. Android would normally pick this
    directory only when the PHONE is set to te, which is not the same as the
    language the user chose in this app. AlarmPrefs.localized() forces the
    configuration from the bridged `language` field so the alarm speaks the app's
    language on an English phone. See AlarmPrefs.kt and BRIDGE_CONTRACT.md.

    Only the FRAME is here. Medication names arrive as %1$s format arguments
    straight from the Room store, exactly as the user typed them — never
    translated, never transliterated.

    Counts stay Western numerals, matching the web (see lib/i18n/format.ts).
    app_name and the URL-scheme strings are deliberately absent: a brand and two
    machine tokens are not words.
-->
